course: dictionary
lesson: 2564
title: Delight and its many uses
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Delight is a feeling of great happiness and pleasure. You can feel delight, and you can also be a delight: a person or thing that gives great pleasure. «She squealed with delight when she opened her present.» Squealing is loud and high, so the words around delight show it is a big, happy feeling.
explain: Delight can also be a verb, a doing word. To delight someone is to make them very happy. «The Mole falls over backwards in delight» shows how much he is pleased: falling over backwards is a big, excited reaction, not a quiet smile. «To my delight» means you are very happy about something that has happened.
explain: Watch the words that come after delight. «Delight in» and «take delight in» mean to enjoy something very much. Sometimes this enjoyment is unkind: a person who takes delight in other people's mistakes enjoys them, and that is not nice. The clues are the words around it, so always read the whole sentence.
fact: Delight means a feeling of great happiness and pleasure.
fact: A delight is someone or something that gives great pleasure.
fact: As a verb, «delight» means to make someone very happy, or to enjoy something very much.
fact: «Turkish delight» is a sweet, so the word can also name a food.
fact: «Red sky at night, shepherd's delight» is a saying about the weather, and it is not always right.
exercise: «She squealed with delight when she opened her present.» What does delight mean here? | Tiredness after a long day | Being cold and wet | Anger at a wrong present | *Great happiness and pleasure
exercise: «The Mole falls over backwards in delight.» What does this show? | The Mole is tired and wants to sleep | *The Mole is overjoyed | The Mole is cross and stamping his feet | The Mole is lost in the wood
exercise: A teacher writes on a report, «a delight to teach». What does she mean? | The pupil has lost a book | The lesson was too hard for everyone | *The pupil is very pleasant and a joy to teach | The pupil is ill and cannot come
exercise: «To my delight, the sun came out.» What does «to my delight» tell you? | *I was very happy about it | I was very angry about it | I was very worried about it | I did not notice it at all
exercise: Which sentence uses delight as a verb? | Delight is a word with two syllables | The delight of the picnic was the cake | *Her kind words will delight her grandma | A delight of sweets sat on the table
test: «He takes delight in winning every game, even when his friends lose.» What does «takes delight in» mean? | Forgets about something | Hides from something | *Enjoys something very much, sometimes in an unkind way | Is afraid of something
test: «Their visit was a delight to everyone.» What is a delight here? | A bad mistake | Something that has been lost | A loud noise in the night | *Something or someone that gives great pleasure
exam: Which sentence uses «delight» correctly to mean great happiness? | The bus was late and the delight was cold | *Her face showed pure delight when the puppy ran to her | The delight of the cake was in the oven | He will delight in the bus timetable on Monday
